  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Krishna Murthy Pabbathi, vs The State Of Telangana on 30 June, 2025 Author: N.Tukaramji Bench: N.Tukaramji The Honourable Sri Justice N.Tukaramji Criminal Petition No. 7990 Of 2025 Order",
    "facts": "This Criminal Petition is filed under Section 528 of Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 (for short 'BNSS, 2023') seeking quashment of the proceedings in F.I.R No.278 of 2025 on the file of Matwada Police Station, Warangal District, against the petitioner/accused. 2. The petitioner is arrayed as sole accused in F.I.R No.130 of 2025 registered for the offences punishable under Sections 272 and 275 of BNS. Accordingly, the complainant apprehended the accused and seized 1) Anaar tobacco 14- boxes 14 x 500 =7000/-, 2) RR tobacco 10-boxes 10 x 500 = 5000/-, 3) Baba Black 09-packets 09 x 300= 2700/-, 4) JK 40-boxes 40-packets 40 x 250 = 10,000/-, 5) RMD 24-packets 24 x 1000=24,000/-, total worth of Rs.48,700/- under confession and seizure panchanama. 3 NTR,J 9.",
    "arguments": "4. The prosecution case in brief is that the petitioner/accused is involved in selling and purchasing the banned Tobacco products and the Police concerned has seized the said Tobacco products worth of Rs.48,700/- from the possession of the petitioner. 5. Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that a Coordinate Bench of this Court vide Criminal Petition Nos.3731 and Batch on considering similar allegations and the merits [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the petitioners therein. He further submits that the police have 2 NTR,J registered the present crime in violation of the orders passed by this Court. Hence, prayed for quashment of the proceedings against the petitioners. 6. Learned Additional Public Prosecutor would submit that the petitioner had been found with the Tobacco products and investigation is pending. However fairly admitted that in the authority cited by the petitioner in the similar circumstances, the proceedings against the petitioner therein were [LEAKAGE_MASK]. 10. Having regard to similar factual position, a Coordinate Bench of this Court in Crl.P.No.6235 of 2022 held that against the allegations of illegal sale and transportation of tobacco products the accusations under Sections 188, 269, 270, 272, 273, 278, 328 read with Sections 511, 336, 409 and 420 of I.P.C., cannot be maintained and [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the petitioners therein.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. The prosecution case in brief is that the petitioner/accused is involved in selling and purchasing the banned Tobacco products and the Police concerned has seized the said Tobacco products worth of Rs.48,700/- from the possession of the petitioner.",
    "respondent_arguments": "5. Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that a Coordinate Bench of this Court vide Criminal Petition Nos.3731 and Batch on considering similar allegations and the merits [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the petitioners therein. He further submits that the police have 2 NTR,J registered the present crime in violation of the orders passed by this Court. Hence, prayed for quashment of the proceedings against the petitioners. 6. Learned Additional Public Prosecutor would submit that the petitioner had been found with the Tobacco products and investigation is pending. However fairly admitted that in the authority cited by the petitioner in the similar circumstances, the proceedings against the petitioner therein were [LEAKAGE_MASK].",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "10. Having regard to similar factual position, a Coordinate Bench of this Court in Crl.P.No.6235 of 2022 held that against the allegations of illegal sale and transportation of tobacco products the accusations under Sections 188, 269, 270, 272, 273, 278, 328 read with Sections 511, 336, 409 and 420 of I.P.C., cannot be maintained and [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the petitioners therein."
  },
